# The GitHub API as the server calls it: relative paths against GitHub:ApiBaseUrl, with the
# caller's bearer token forwarded on every request.
@apiBaseUrl = https://api.github.com/
@token = replace-with-a-github-token

### REST: the authenticated user
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}user
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### GraphQL: the authenticated user's login (always POST; never retried)
# On GitHub Enterprise Server (apiBaseUrl = https://<host>/api/v3/) GraphQL is the sibling
# https://<host>/api/graphql, not {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { viewer { login } }",
  "variables": {}
}

### GraphQL: list projects linked to a repository (finds the board titled Workflow)
# Repeat with "after" set to pageInfo.endCursor while pageInfo.hasNextPage is true.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$after:String){ repository(owner:$owner,name:$name){ projectsV2(first: 100, after:$after){ nodes{ id number title closed resourcePath } pageInfo{ hasNextPage endCursor } } } }",
  "variables": {
    "owner": "credfeto",
    "name": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "after": null
  }
}

### GraphQL: a pull request's review decision, comments, reviews and review threads (pr_comments)
# Each connection is paged on its own: while one still has pageInfo.hasNextPage true, repeat with its
# include flag true and its "...After" set to its pageInfo.endCursor; finished connections get false.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!,$n:Int!,$comments:Boolean!,$reviews:Boolean!,$threads:Boolean!,$commentsAfter:String,$reviewsAfter:String,$threadsAfter:String){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){pullRequest(number:$n){reviewDecision comments(first:100,after:$commentsAfter) @include(if:$comments){totalCount pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor} nodes{fullDatabaseId author{__typename login} authorAssociation createdAt isMinimized url body}} reviews(first:100,after:$reviewsAfter) @include(if:$reviews){totalCount pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor} nodes{fullDatabaseId author{__typename login} authorAssociation state submittedAt url body}} reviewThreads(first:100,after:$threadsAfter) @include(if:$threads){totalCount pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor} nodes{isResolved isOutdated path line originalLine comments(first:100){totalCount pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor} nodes{fullDatabaseId author{__typename login} authorAssociation createdAt isMinimized url body replyTo{fullDatabaseId} pullRequestReview{fullDatabaseId}}}}}}}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "n": 41,
    "comments": true,
    "reviews": true,
    "threads": true,
    "commentsAfter": null,
    "reviewsAfter": null,
    "threadsAfter": null
  }
}

### GraphQL: the issues a pull request closes, with their labels (closing_issue_labels)
# While closingIssuesReferences.pageInfo.hasNextPage is true, repeat with "after" set to its endCursor.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!,$n:Int!,$after:String){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){pullRequest(number:$n){closingIssuesReferences(first:100,after:$after){pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor} nodes{number repository{owner{login} name} labels(first:100){pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor} nodes{name}}}}}}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "n": 98,
    "after": null
  }
}

### GraphQL: the next page of a closing issue's labels, only when its labels had another page (closing_issue_labels)
# Uses the issue's own repository, which can differ from the pull request's; repeat while hasNextPage is true.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!,$n:Int!,$after:String){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){issue(number:$n){labels(first:100,after:$after){pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor} nodes{name}}}}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "n": 14,
    "after": null
  }
}

### GraphQL: a pull request's default fields, every field except files and body (pr_view)
# The query only selects the requested fields; $after is declared only when commit-authors is requested.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!,$n:Int!,$after:String){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){pullRequest(number:$n){state isDraft title url baseRefName headRefName headRefOid autoMergeRequest{enabledAt} reviewDecision mergeStateStatus mergeable createdAt merged mergedAt merged mergeCommit{oid} labels(first:100){totalCount nodes{name}} assignees(first:100){totalCount nodes{login}} author{login} commits(first:100,after:$after){totalCount pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor} nodes{commit{authors(first:100){totalCount nodes{user{login}}}}}}}}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "n": 41,
    "after": null
  }
}

### GraphQL: the next page of a pull request's commit authors (pr_view commit-authors)
# Repeat with "after" set to commits.pageInfo.endCursor while commits.pageInfo.hasNextPage is true.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!,$n:Int!,$after:String){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){pullRequest(number:$n){commits(first:100,after:$after){totalCount pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor} nodes{commit{authors(first:100){totalCount nodes{user{login}}}}}}}}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "n": 41,
    "after": "replace-with-the-previous-end-cursor"
  }
}

### GraphQL: a pull request's changed file count, read before listing the files (pr_view files)
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!,$n:Int!){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){pullRequest(number:$n){changedFiles}}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "n": 41
  }
}

### GraphQL: a pull request's body, which can only be asked for on its own (pr_view body)
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!,$n:Int!){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){pullRequest(number:$n){body}}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "n": 41
  }
}

### GraphQL: an issue's or pull request's status on the Workflow board (board_read_status, workflow_status_check)
# For a pull request use item:pullRequest(number:$n) in place of item:issue(number:$n). The node whose project id is
# the board's gives the status: the legacy "Workflow Status" field wins, else "Status" when it is a workflow state.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!,$n:Int!){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){item:issue(number:$n){projectItems(first:100){nodes{project{id} legacy:fieldValueByName(name:\"Workflow Status\"){... on ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue{name}} status:fieldValueByName(name:\"Status\"){... on ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue{name}}} pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "n": 7
  }
}

### GraphQL: list the Workflow board's items, only after the direct status read failed (board_read_status, workflow_status_check)
# Repeat with "c" set to pageInfo.endCursor while pageInfo.hasNextPage is true and the work item is not yet found.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($project:ID!,$c:String){node(id:$project){... on ProjectV2{items(first:100,after:$c){nodes{type content{... on Issue{number repository{nameWithOwner}} ... on PullRequest{number repository{nameWithOwner}}} legacy:fieldValueByName(name:\"Workflow Status\"){... on ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue{name}} status:fieldValueByName(name:\"Status\"){... on ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue{name}}} pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}}}",
  "variables": {
    "project": "PVT_kwDOA",
    "c": null
  }
}

### GraphQL: a work item's node id, only when its board item id is not cached (board_set_status, workflow_status_set, issue_create)
# For a pull request use item:pullRequest(number:$n) in place of item:issue(number:$n).
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!,$n:Int!){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){item:issue(number:$n){id}}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp",
    "n": 6
  }
}

### GraphQL: add a work item to the Workflow board (board_set_status, workflow_status_set, issue_create)
# Adding an item that is already on the board returns its existing item id.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($p:ID!,$c:ID!){addProjectV2ItemById(input:{projectId:$p,contentId:$c}){item{id}}}",
  "variables": {
    "p": "PVT_kwDOA",
    "c": "I_kwDOA"
  }
}

### GraphQL: set a board item's status (board_set_status, workflow_status_set, issue_create)
# An error saying "Could not resolve to a node" means the cached item id is stale, so the item is added again.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation($p:ID!,$i:ID!,$f:ID!,$o:String!){updateProjectV2ItemFieldValue(input:{projectId:$p,itemId:$i,fieldId:$f,value:{singleSelectOptionId:$o}}){projectV2Item{id}}}",
  "variables": {
    "p": "PVT_kwDOA",
    "i": "PVTI_lADOA",
    "f": "PVTSSF_lADOA",
    "o": "47fc9ee4"
  }
}

### GraphQL: the Workflow board's single-select fields and their options (board_set_status, workflow_status_set, issue_create)
# A legacy "Workflow Status" field takes precedence over the built-in "Status" field. Fields of other
# types arrive as empty objects because they do not match the inline fragment.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($projectId:ID!){node(id:$projectId){... on ProjectV2{fields(first:100){nodes{... on ProjectV2SingleSelectField{id name options{id name}}}}}}}",
  "variables": {
    "projectId": "PVT_kwDOA"
  }
}

### GraphQL: a repository's visibility (leak check for references in text written to a repository, body_check)
# The only GitHub request body_check makes: first for the repository the body is for, and only when the body
# references another repository, then for each referenced repository whose owner is not a private owner.
# Visibility is PUBLIC, PRIVATE or INTERNAL. An error saying "Could not resolve to a Repository" means the
# repository is missing or the caller cannot see it. The REST equivalent is the visibility field of
# GET repos/{owner}/{repo}.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query($o:String!,$r:String!){repository(owner:$o,name:$r){visibility}}",
  "variables": {
    "o": "credfeto",
    "r": "credfeto-workflow-mcp"
  }
}

### REST: a branch's head and its classic branch protection required checks (branch_required_checks)
# A '#' in the branch name is sent as %23; '/' is sent as is. A 404 means the branch or the repository
# is missing, which the repository request below tells apart.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/branches/main
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: the ruleset rules that apply to a branch (branch_required_checks)
# Follow the Link header's rel="next" URL until there is none. A 403 saying "Upgrade to GitHub Pro or
# make this repository public" means rulesets are unavailable, so the branch has no ruleset checks.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/rules/branches/main?per_page=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: the repository, only after the branch request returned 404 (branch_required_checks)
# A 200 means the branch is missing; a 404 means the repository is missing or the caller cannot see it.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: a pull request's changed files, after reading the changed file count (pr_view files)
# Follow the Link header's rel="next" URL until there is none. The call fails rather than return a partial
# list when fewer files are listed than the changedFiles count.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/pulls/41/files?per_page=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: a repository's open pull requests (pr_list)
# Follow the Link header's rel="next" URL until there is none. The head, issue and label filters are applied
# to the listed pull requests, and the call is refused when more than 1000 remain after the head filter.
# A 404 means the repository is missing or the caller cannot see it.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/pulls?state=open&per_page=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: an issue's title, state, labels, assignees and body (issue_view)
# GitHub serves pull requests from this endpoint too; a response with a pull_request link is reported as
# no such issue. A 404 means the issue or the repository is missing, or the caller cannot see it.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/issues/16
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: an issue's labels, for the Blocked flag (issue_plan_status)
# A response with a pull_request link, or an html_url ending /pull/{number}, is reported as no such issue.
# A 404 means the issue or the repository is missing, or the caller cannot see it.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/issues/17
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: an issue's comments, oldest first, to find the latest implementation plan (issue_plan_status)
# Follow the Link header's rel="next" URL until there is none. Comment bodies are read but never returned.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/issues/17/comments?per_page=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: a repository's open issues (issue_list)
# Follow the Link header's rel="next" URL until there is none. GitHub serves pull requests from this endpoint too;
# an item with a pull_request member is skipped, and the call is refused when more than 1000 issues remain.
# A 404 means the repository is missing or the caller cannot see it.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/issues?state=open&per_page=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: search a repository's issue titles and bodies for text (issue_search)
# q is "in:title,body <words> repo:<owner/repo> type:issue", plus "state:open" or "state:closed" unless every state
# is wanted, URL-encoded as one value. per_page is the limit plus one, at most 100, so a further match shows the
# result is truncated, as does a total_count above the limit. A 404 means the repository is missing, or the caller
# cannot see it.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}search/issues?q=in%3Atitle%2Cbody%20issue%20search%20repo%3Acredfeto%2Fcredfeto-workflow-mcp%20type%3Aissue%20state%3Aopen&per_page=31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: search a repository's pull request titles and bodies for text (pr_search)
# q is "in:title,body <words> repo:<owner/repo> type:pr", plus "state:open", "state:closed" or "is:merged" unless
# every state is wanted, URL-encoded as one value. "state:closed" includes merged pull requests. per_page is the
# limit plus one, at most 100, so a further match shows the result is truncated, as does a total_count above the
# limit. A 404 means the repository is missing, or the caller cannot see it.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}search/issues?q=in%3Atitle%2Cbody%20search%20repo%3Acredfeto%2Fcredfeto-workflow-mcp%20type%3Apr%20state%3Aopen&per_page=31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: the repository, read before searching its code (code_search)
# Code search answers 422 for a repository that is missing, so the repository is read first: a 404 means it is
# missing or the caller cannot see it.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: search a repository's default branch code for text, with the matched fragments (code_search)
# q is "<words> repo:<owner/repo>", URL-encoded as one value. The text-match media type returns each file's
# text_matches, whose matches are counted. per_page is the limit plus one, at most 100, so a further match shows
# the result is truncated, as does a total_count above the limit. The files are sorted by path.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}search/code?q=McpServerTool%20repo%3Acredfeto%2Fcredfeto-workflow-mcp&per_page=31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github.text-match+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: search an owner's repository names and descriptions for text (repo_search)
# q is "in:name,description <words> user:<owner>", plus "archived:false" unless archived repositories are wanted,
# URL-encoded as one value; "user:" matches organisations too. per_page is the limit plus one, at most 100, so a
# further match shows the result is truncated, as does a total_count above the limit. A 422 means the owner is
# missing, or the caller cannot search it. The repositories are sorted by name.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}search/repositories?q=in%3Aname%2Cdescription%20workflow%20user%3Acredfeto%20archived%3Afalse&per_page=31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: a repository's labels, before creating the missing ones (issue_create)
# Read in full, following the Link header's next page; a label is matched without regard to case.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/labels?per_page=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: create a missing standard label with its standard colour and description (issue_create)
# A label that is not a standard one is sent with only its name, so GitHub picks the colour. A 422 whose errors
# include the code already_exists means another caller created it meanwhile, which is not an error.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/labels
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Read Me","color":"5319e7","description":"Repository readme file"}

### REST: create the issue with its priority label first, then the other labels (issue_create)
# Its html_url must match https://<host>[:<port>]/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<number>; neither the host nor the
# repository is compared. It is then put on the Workflow board as Not Started with the GraphQL requests above.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/issues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"docs: try the issue_create tool","body":"## Summary\n\nCreated from docs/github.http.","labels":["Medium","Enhancement","Read Me"]}

### REST: an inline review comment, read before replying to it (pr_reply)
# pull_request_url names the pull request the comment belongs to; in_reply_to_id, when present, is the
# thread's top comment, which the reply goes to. A 404 means the comment or the repository is missing.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/pulls/comments/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: reply in an inline review comment's thread (pr_reply; never retried)
# The comment id is the thread's top comment. A 400, 401, 403, 404, 410 or 422 means the reply was not
# posted; any other failure means it may have been posted, so check with pr_comments before trying again.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/pulls/87/comments/1/replies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Fixed in abc1234: the reply text."
}

### REST: post a top-level comment on a pull request or an issue (comment_add; never retried)
# A pull request's conversation comments are issue comments, so this takes either number. The html_url names
# /pull/ or /issues/ whichever GitHub answers with. A 400, 401, 403, 404, 410 or 422 means the comment was not
# posted; any other failure means it may have been posted, so check with issue_comments before trying again.
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/issues/31/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "## Summary\n\nPosted from docs/github.http."
}

### REST: a repository's workflow runs on a branch or commit, when no workflow is given (run_list)
# One page only: per_page is the limit, at most 50. The filter is branch=<branch>, with the name URL-encoded, or
# head_sha=<sha>; no event filter is set, so runs of every trigger are listed. Every run returned must match the
# filter, and the runs are sorted newest first. A 404 means the repository is missing or the caller cannot see it.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/actions/runs?branch=main&per_page=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: a repository's workflows, to find the one given by file name or name (run_list)
# Follow the Link header's rel="next" URL until there is none. A workflow is matched by the file name at the end
# of its path first, then by its name; a disabled workflow is still listed, so its runs can be read.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/actions/workflows?per_page=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: one workflow's runs on a branch or commit, after finding its id (run_list)
# The same filter, limit and checks as the repository's workflow runs above, with the id from the workflows list.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/actions/workflows/1/runs?branch=main&per_page=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: a workflow run, with its latest attempt number (run_view, run_log)
# The id must match the run asked for and run_attempt must be at least 1. GitHub answers 404 for a missing
# repository and a missing run alike, so on a 404 the repository is read with GET repos/{owner}/{repo} to tell
# them apart.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/actions/runs/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: the jobs of a run's latest attempt (run_view, run_log)
# Follow the Link header's rel="next" URL until there is none. Only the latest attempt is read, so a job from an
# earlier attempt never hides the current result. The list is refused as incomplete when the number of jobs read
# differs from total_count, when total_count changes between pages, or when it is above 1000.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/actions/runs/1/attempts/1/jobs?per_page=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp

### REST: the log archive of a run's latest attempt, only when a job failed (run_log)
# GitHub answers 302 with a short-lived signed Location URL for the zip archive; the redirect is not followed. The
# archive is downloaded from that URL without the token, only over https on the default port and only from
# results-receiver.actions.githubusercontent.com or a productionresultssa<n>.blob.core.windows.net host, again
# without following redirects. A 404 means the logs were not found and a 410 that they are past their retention.
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}repos/credfeto/credfeto-workflow-mcp/actions/runs/1/attempts/1/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2026-03-10
User-Agent: credfeto-workflow-mcp
